---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const updated = 'August 2026';
const supportEmail = 'yash@typethink.ai';
---

<AppLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — doodleai.art"
	description="How doodleai.art handles accounts, chats, images, browser storage, analytics, and the services that help run Doodle AI."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
			<h1>Privacy <span class="grad">Policy</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Doodle AI keeps browsing open, but you sign in when you want to create, save, and sync doodles.
				Generation runs through account credits and a server-owned PicX connection.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

			<h2>The short version</h2>
			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Accounts</div><div class="v">Google sign-in for creation</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Selling data</div><div class="v">Never</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Ad pixels</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Cookies</div><div class="v">Analytics (DataFast + GA4)</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Generation</div><div class="v">Platform credits</div></div>
			</div>

			<h2>What we collect</h2>
			<p>
				You can browse and create without an account. If you choose Google sign-in, Doodle AI receives the
				basic profile information Google shares for authentication, such as your name, email address, and
				profile image. We also create authentication and session records so you can stay signed in securely.
			</p>
			<p>
				When you are signed in, we store the Doodle AI content needed to sync your workspace: chat thread
				metadata and messages, generated-image references, saved moodboard items, saved characters, and
				generation metadata such as the selected skill, prompt, status, and credit usage. This content is
				scoped to your account.
			</p>

			<h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Signed out:</b> chats and interface preferences may remain in your browser's local storage, but image generation and uploads require a signed-in account.</li>
				<li><b>Signed in:</b> your browser keeps a local mirror so the interface is responsive, while supported chats, boards, characters, and generation data are synchronized to your account for access on your other devices.</li>
				<li><b>Credentials:</b> Provider credentials stay on the server and are not sent to your browser.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How your content is processed</h2>
			<p>
				When you send a chat message, the message and relevant conversation context are sent to the language
				model service that powers the Doodle AI agent. When you attach a photo or request an image, the
				photo, reference assets, prompt, and generation settings are sent to PicX through Doodle AI's
				server-owned connection. PicX hosts the resulting media and returns URLs that Doodle AI can display
				or save. Each generation is charged against the signed-in account's credit balance.
			</p>
			<p>
				Do not upload anything you do not have the right to use. The privacy practices of PicX and the model
				provider also apply to the information you send to those services.
			</p>

			<h2>Who helps run Doodle AI</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Cloudflare</b> — hosts the site, API, D1 database, and session storage.</li>
				<li><b>Google</b> — provides optional Google OAuth sign-in. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
				<li><b>PicX</b> — processes image-generation requests, manages uploaded assets, and hosts generated media through Doodle AI's platform account.</li>
				<li><b>OpenRouter</b> — routes chat requests to the language model used by the Doodle AI agent.</li>
				<li><b>DataFast</b> — provides website analytics about visits, referrals, pages, and general device, browser, and country-level information.</li>
				<li><b>Mixpanel</b> — provides product event analytics (sign-up, generation, skill usage) and user profiles. See <a href="https://mixpanel.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mixpanel's privacy policy</a>.</li>
				<li><b>Google Analytics</b> — provides traffic analysis, session measurement, and audience insights. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
			<p>
				We use three analytics services to understand how people find and use the site:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><b><a href="https://datafa.st" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataFast</a></b> — pageview analytics (visits, referrals, device and country info). Uses cookies to recognise returning visitors.</li>
				<li><b><a href="https://mixpanel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mixpanel</a></b> — product event tracking (sign-up, generation, skill selection) and anonymous user profiles linked by internal ID. Uses localStorage, not cookies.</li>
				<li><b><a href="https://analytics.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics 4</a></b> — traffic sources, sessions, engagement, and audience demographics. Uses cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>).</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not run advertising pixels, participate in an ad network, or sell analytics data. You can
				block or clear analytics cookies in your browser settings; the site should continue to work without
				them. See each provider's privacy policy linked above for their processing details.
			</p>

			<h2>Server logs and security</h2>
			<p>
				Our hosting and security providers may process standard request information such as IP address,
				user agent, timestamps, and request details to deliver the site, maintain security, and investigate
				abuse. We do not use server logs to build advertising profiles. No internet service can guarantee
				absolute security, but we use access controls and account scoping to protect stored data.
			</p>

			<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
			<div class="callout">
				<p>
					Signed-out browser data can be removed by clearing site data for doodleai.art. Signed-in users can
					remove individual chats, moodboard items, and characters in the app. To request deletion of your
					Doodle AI account and associated server-side content, email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
					from the account email address. Data held by PicX, Google, OpenRouter, Cloudflare, or DataFast is
					subject to that provider's own retention and deletion practices.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				Doodle AI is not directed at children. If you believe a child has provided personal information to
				us, please contact us so we can review and remove it where appropriate.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If our data practices change, we will update this page and the date at the top. Your continued use
				of Doodle AI after an update means you acknowledge the revised policy.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Privacy questions or deletion requests:
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Back to the app</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
